//! name: ir_verify_secret_fields
//! rule: 05.R6
//! expect: parse-ok
//! detail: IR-ONLY -- every FMIR/OIR/LIR value's secret bit and `ct_region` id are non-optional fields lowering always fills in; a Fors program has no syntax to omit them -- pinned by crates/fors-fmir/tests/negative_corpus/01-missing-secret-field.fmir and 02-missing-ct-region.fmir (DiagCode::MissingSecretField/MissingCtRegion), run by verify.rs's missing_secret_field_is_rejected and missing_ct_region_is_rejected. This is the smallest legal program carrying a secret-typed value end to end.

module ir_verify_secret_fields;
needs { };

fn identity(let s: secret u64) -> secret u64 {
    return s;
}
